{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791298801,"nonce":"V0SnmikCTjlH9MIha+KeFzk6lVM=","title":"Anonymous Dynamic fields are mislabeled as String and boxed twice on reflection","message":"At cfdca1d4d56fe698e6345b6541f1fde72d66a8ea (857/1094), MIR runtime_type_id maps TypeKind::Dynamic to the String tag 5. Anonymous literals use this value in their shape descriptor while storing a DynamicValue pointer. rayzor_anon_get_field then treats that pointer as a raw HaxeString and boxes it again. Reflect.field/copy and constrained field reads see an address or dereference a DynamicValue as a String.\n\nReproducer DynamicObjectFields.hx: object(value:Dynamic):{value:Dynamic} returns {value:value}. Its first check with Int 5 crashes under Rayzor; native Haxe passes. It exercises primitive, null, String and Array payloads, reflected/copy reads, mutation, and values merged from structural generic parameters. Baseline log /tmp/rayzor-dynamic-fields-before.log. MIR evidence for TestConstrainedMonomorphs /tmp/rayzor-merged-constraints-mir.log: merge has shape bar:5,foo:5 and stores pointers returned by haxe_reflect_field; the caller gets a doubly boxed String-tagged foo and reports its address instead of 5.\n\nDynamic storage needs its own slot tag, and reflection must preserve its already-boxed payload. The existing Dynamic type token is TYPE_DYNAMIC_TOKEN (u32::MAX - 2), separate from String. Keep class/anonymous/reference boxing tags consistent and measure the full corpus for effects beyond the isolated reproducer. Generic return-constraint inference and missing-field macro probes in TestConstrainedMonomorphs remain separate.","files":null}]}